---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="MEAL & Impact Evaluation"
  description="MEAL systems and impact evaluation for development, ESG and value-chain programmes."
>
  <section class="section service-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/#what-we-do">&larr; What We Do</a></p>
      <h1>Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability &amp; Learning</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We design and run MEAL systems and impact evaluations for
        organisations working on sustainable development, ESG and
        responsible value chains, giving funders, implementing partners and
        communities a clear, credible view of what a programme is actually
        achieving.
      </p>

      <div class="body-grid">
        <div>
          <h2>What this covers</h2>
          <p>
            We build MEAL frameworks from the ground up: theory of change,
            indicators, data collection tools and reporting rhythms sized to
            the programme itself. For programmes already underway, we can
            step in as an independent evaluator, running baseline, midline or
            endline studies and assessing outcomes against the original
            programme design.
          </p>
          <p>
            We also support ESG and value-chain due diligence work: risk
            assessments, verification of claims made along a supply chain,
            and monitoring frameworks for responsible sourcing commitments,
            including in artisanal and small-scale mining contexts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>How we work</h2>
          <p>
            We keep evaluation independent from implementation. That means
            we typically work alongside the organisation running the
            programme on the ground. This keeps findings credible to funders
            and communities alike.
          </p>
          <p>
            Every engagement ends with something usable: a results
            framework, a report written for the audience that needs to act
            on it, and, where useful, a short learning session with the
            programme team to walk through what the findings mean in
            practice.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="/contact">Talk to us about your programme</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-page .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .service-page .eyebrow a {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .body-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--gap);
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .cta-row {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(40, 40, 40, 0.1);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .body-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
